        <mxCell id="UrCkISKYRLRXjf0qk5b_-84" value="200OK: User receives his / her Account-information with authentication&lt;div&gt;400BadRequest:&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;User only receives generic error-response, so it won&#39;t help attackers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Input for all endpoints will be validated in the controller-class with ModelState.isValid. It will only create unnecessary confusion to add it to the business logic and it won&#39;t be tested in unit-tests either&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*CheckPasswordsMatch(password1, password2): takes password from loginDto and from Account with matching email compare those values. The method is places in a ServiceHelper-class&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*GenerateJWT(account): generate JWT token with claims and return JWT token or &quot;&quot;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=note;size=20;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;verticalAlign=top;" parent="1" vertex="1">
